& [DocumentRoleFamilyInventory] distinguishes source meaning from execution
  + [source_document] preserves dictated or imported language and never becomes derived authority by rewriting
  + [definition] declares semantic identities, terms, relations, and interpretation rules
  + [data] records facts, observations, quotations, indexes, manifests, states, and evidence
  + [contract] declares preconditions, invariants, effects, outputs, faults, and termination
  + [program] explicitly composes admitted operations under a declared execution profile
  + [policy] governs authority, trust, privacy, safety, lifecycle, validation, or admission
  + [profile] narrows a general language, runtime, provider, platform, or target contract
  + [test_or_fixture] supplies controlled input and expected behavior without acquiring production authority
  + [proof] records observed verification and limitations without changing the governed subject
  + [narrative] preserves history, reasoning, reentry, attribution, and unresolved frontier
  + [mixed] contains multiple roles whose boundaries must be explicitly delimited before any program region is executable
  = must: treat program execution as opt-in through explicit document and region roles
  - never: treat valid SOP syntax, a signature, an instruction-shaped sentence, or file location alone as execution admission

& [ExistingLanguageAndRuntimeSupport] is substantial but bounded
  + [language_identity] is formed by SOP Semantic Programming Identity and SOP Core
  + [attention_and_inference] is formed by the attention-first foundation, faculty attention language, reflective VM, and inference-frame profiles
  + [semantic_data] is formed by semantic fabric graph, ontology profiles, definitions, trusted source spans, and exact indexes
  + [program_and_transition] is formed by instruction, program, state, transition, faculty cycle, task, and bounded effect contracts
  + [trust_and_package] is implemented through source digests, signed packages, admission, revocation, dependency locks, and exact query proof
  + [runtime_surfaces] are bounded CLI, MCP, service, ecosystem, and Windows preflight crates
  + [self_hosting] is bounded source ingestion and reviewed corpus construction rather than general language self-compilation
  + [gap] is no one canonical document-role registry or general source-to-multi-target language implementation

& [TargetMaturityMatrix] is current-role evidence
  + [SOP-X_exact] is implemented_bounded for normalized exact query, validation, transition, package, CLI, MCP, service, and selected faculty forms
  + [SOP-N_neural] is formed_not_implemented for neural blueprint, routing, gating, initialization, calibration, training, and package semantics
  + [SOP-H_hybrid] is formed_and_partially_probed through exact gates around provider candidates but lacks a general target ABI and conformance proof
  + [SOP-A_attention] is formed as model-visible frames and directives but lacks one canonical compilation target profile
  + [SOP-D_data] is formed_and_bounded_implemented through semantic records, relations, indexes, packages, and query surfaces
  + [SOP-T_tools] is bounded_implemented through CLI, MCP, service, tool discovery, and addressed interfaces
  + [SOP-W_workflow] is formed through faculty, planner, task, reflection, and supervision contracts with partial bounded runtime support
  + [SOP-F_hardware] is exploratory_specification_only for bytecode, FPGA interpreter, or native hardware compilation
  + [SOP-I_inspection] is formed_and_implemented_bounded through verified quotes, paths, explanations, diagnostics, manifests, and proofs
  = must: preserve maturity and authority per target instead of describing the whole matrix as implemented

& [CompatibilityInventory] preserves current meaning
  + existing data, definitions, source quotations, manifests, narratives, and proofs remain non-executable unless an explicit future role contract says otherwise
  + existing programs remain governed by the exact profile and authority under which they were signed
  + unsupported historic forms remain preserved and cannot be silently reinterpreted by the multi-target purpose
  + exact target behavior remains the fallback and authority substrate for supported deterministic semantics
  + neural and hybrid targets remain proposal-bound and cannot hold authoritative meaning or permission only in weights
  + purpose revision requires reversible migration records for any file whose role or lowering changes

& [AuthorityInventory] explains why SMTC remains upstream
  + current signed specifications retain their bounded authority
  + the dictated multi-target purpose has no canonical, implementation, migration, or default-execution authority
  + 72 observed top-level specifications contain signature status beginning with valid, but their scopes differ and must not be flattened
  + 4 observed top-level specifications are superseded and remain historical lineage rather than current authority
  + 2 observed top-level specifications lack the SJS protocol UUID and require governance review before any current-authority claim
  + target maturity does not grant target activation authority

